{"from": "claim:mk-11-02-03-unridden-colt", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:jesus-of-nazareth"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-02-03-unridden-colt", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-21-02-03-donkey-and-colt-fetched", "note": "Matthew has a donkey with its colt (two animals, per Matthew's reading of Zechariah 9:9); Mark has one young donkey (polos), on which no one had ever sat."}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-09-10-coming-kingdom-of-david", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:jesus-of-nazareth"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-09-10-coming-kingdom-of-david", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:david"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-09-10-coming-kingdom-of-david", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-21-09-hosanna-acclamation", "note": "Mark's crowd acclaims 'the kingdom of our father David that is coming'; Matthew's acclaims 'Hosanna to the son of David' - a wording difference, not a contradiction."}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-09-10-coming-kingdom-of-david", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:psalm-118-25-26", "note": "The acclamation 'Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord' quotes Psalm 118:26 (Mark 11:9)."}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-11-temple-looked-around-evening", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:jesus-of-nazareth"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-11-temple-looked-around-evening", "type": "mentions", "to": "place:temple-mount"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-11-temple-looked-around-evening", "type": "mentions", "to": "place:bethany"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-11-temple-looked-around-evening", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-21-12-cleansing-the-temple", "note": "Mark splits the entry and the cleansing over two days (look around on the entry day, cleanse the next morning); Matthew has both in one visit to the Temple."}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-11-temple-looked-around-evening", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-21-17-bethany-lodging", "note": "Mark's evening departure to Bethany (11:11, 11:19) is the nightly lodging Matthew 21:17 reports."}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-13-fig-tree-not-the-season", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-21-18-20-fig-tree-withered", "note": "The same tree and cursing; Mark alone adds that 'it was not the season for figs' and spreads the finding of the withered tree over a second morning."}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-16-no-vessels-through-temple", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:jesus-of-nazareth"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-16-no-vessels-through-temple", "type": "mentions", "to": "place:temple-mount"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-17-house-of-prayer-all-nations", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:jesus-of-nazareth"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-17-house-of-prayer-all-nations", "type": "mentions", "to": "place:temple-mount"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-17-house-of-prayer-all-nations", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-21-13-house-of-prayer-quote", "note": "Mark preserves the Isaiah 56:7 phrase 'for all the nations'; Matthew quotes the verse without it. Both join it to Jeremiah 7:11's 'den of robbers'."}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-17-house-of-prayer-all-nations", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:isaiah-56-7"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-17-house-of-prayer-all-nations", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:jeremiah-7-11"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-18-leaders-sought-to-destroy", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:jesus-of-nazareth"}
{"from": "claim:mk-11-18-leaders-sought-to-destroy", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-21-45-46-leaders-perceived", "note": "The leaders' fear of the crowds recurs in both accounts (Matthew 21:46, Mark 11:18, 12:12); Matthew ties it to perceiving the parables, Mark to the temple teaching and the crowd's astonishment."}
{"from": "observation:fig-breba-crop", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-11-13-fig-tree-not-the-season", "grade": "C", "note": "The fig's main crop develops on the current year's shoots and ripens in late summer or fall, so in spring a fig tree out of leaf-fruit is 'not the season for figs'; the breba (early) crop forms in spring on last year's shoots, so the note does not attest that no early figs were possible - only that the season statement is botanically coherent."}
{"from": "text:psalms-of-solomon-17", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-11-09-10-coming-kingdom-of-david", "grade": "C", "note": "A 1st-century BCE Jewish psalm asks God to 'raise up unto them their king, the son of David' - the Davidic-kingdom expectation in Judea that the crowd's acclamation presupposes. It attests the expectation, never that the crowd spoke these words."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-berakhot-9-5", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-11-16-no-vessels-through-temple", "grade": "B", "note": "Berakhot 9:5 rules out using the Temple as a shortcut - 'One may not make the Temple a shortcut to pass through it' - the institution Mark 11:16 presupposes (carrying a vessel through the courts). Redacted c. 200 CE, so it may not describe the practice of the 30s CE exactly."}
{"from": "artifact:great-isaiah-scroll", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-11-17-house-of-prayer-all-nations", "grade": "C", "note": "The Great Isaiah Scroll (1QIsa-a, ca. 125 BCE) contains the entire Book of Isaiah, including chapter 56 - it carries Isaiah 56:7, the source of the quotation, in a pre-Christian manuscript. It attests the quotation's source text, never that Jesus spoke the words. Regraded B to C by reviewer 5: the claim covers the whole of Mark 11:17, a combined quotation (Isaiah 56:7 with Jeremiah 7:11's 'den of robbers'), and the scroll carries only the Isaiah half - the binding rule grades partial quotations C, on the architect's own Mark 1:2-3 precedent."}
